## Documentation

For comprehensive documentation, visit [docs.konnektr.io/docs/db-query-operator](https://docs.konnektr.io/docs/db-query-operator)

## Quick Start

Install the operator:

```bash
helm install db-query-operator \
  oci://ghcr.io/konnektr-io/charts/{{ template "chart.name" . }} \
  --version {{ template "chart.version" . }} \
  --namespace dbqo-system \
  --create-namespace \
  --set gvkPattern="v1/ConfigMap;apps/v1/Deployment"
```

## Prerequisites

- Kubernetes 1.24+
- Helm 3.8+
- PostgreSQL database accessible from the cluster
- [cert-manager](https://cert-manager.io) for the admission webhook certificate (enabled by default; install with `--set webhook.enabled=false` to skip it)

## Configuration

The `gvkPattern` parameter is required and specifies which Kubernetes resource types the operator can manage.

### Format

`<group>/<version>/<Kind>` or `<version>/<Kind>` for core resources

### Examples

```bash
# Core resources
--set gvkPattern="v1/ConfigMap;v1/Secret;v1/Service"

# Applications
--set gvkPattern="apps/v1/Deployment;apps/v1/StatefulSet"

# ArgoCD Applications
--set gvkPattern="argoproj.io/v1alpha1/Application"

# Multiple types
--set gvkPattern="v1/ConfigMap;apps/v1/Deployment;argoproj.io/v1alpha1/Application"
```

### Admission Validation (Webhook)

The chart installs a validating admission webhook, so an invalid `DatabaseQueryResource` is
rejected when it is created or updated instead of failing later during reconciliation:

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| `spec.pollInterval` | must parse as a Go duration (`30s`, `5m`, `1h30m`) and be greater than zero |
| `spec.database.connectionSecretRef.name` | must not be empty |
| `spec.query` | must not be empty or whitespace only |
| `spec.template` | must not be empty and must parse as a Go template with the operator's function set |
| `spec.statusUpdateQueryTemplate` | when set, must parse as a Go template |
| `spec.changeDetection.changePollInterval` | when set, must parse as a Go duration and be greater than zero |

The chart creates the webhook `Service`, the `ValidatingWebhookConfiguration` and — using
cert-manager — a self-signed `Issuer` plus the serving `Certificate` (stored in the
`webhook-server-cert` Secret, mounted into the operator pod). cert-manager must be installed in
the cluster. Point `webhook.certManager.issuerRef` at an existing issuer to use that instead of
the self-signed one.

Because the webhook is installed with `failurePolicy: Fail`, creating and updating
`DatabaseQueryResource` objects is rejected while the webhook is unreachable. To run without
admission validation:

```bash
--set webhook.enabled=false
```

